    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with an aggressive outfield configuration, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (82.82) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.87), who represent our strongest offensive engines. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive +19% bump due to the favorable SP_xERA of 5.19 against Jack Kochanowicz, providing the highest ceiling of the day. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a top-tier start; despite facing Zack Littell, his 18% SP skill advantage and elite status as a dual-threat asset make him an automatic lock, even if his 60% SB hold rate is slightly neutralized by a quick-to-the-plate opposing catcher. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.69) also project well, with **Jackson Merrill**'s +10% order bonus at the top of the lineup helping him overcome a slight park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Coby Mayo** (51.44), who fell just shy of cracking the starting nine. While **Coby Mayo** offers significant power potential against Zack Littell, his projected #7 spot in the order significantly depressed his efficiency score compared to the bottom-tier starters like **Brady House** (56.25). **Brady House** earns the nod over **Coby Mayo** primarily due to the 90% stolen base opportunity created by the slow delivery of Shane Baz, prioritizing the scarcity of speed over raw slugging potential in this specific matchup. Meanwhile, **Josh Jung** (59.79) narrowly makes the cut as our Utility option, benefiting from an favorable matchup against Spencer Arrighetti (4.92 xERA).\n\nStrategic caution is advised regarding several lineup-pending statuses, specifically for **Sam Antonacci**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**. While their scores reflect the assumed batting order, any demotion in those spots\u2014particularly for **Sam Antonacci** at the top of the order\u2014could shift their value downward. Furthermore, **Drake Baldwin** faces a tough test against Connelly Early (2.92 xERA), keeping his score at a modest 46.72; he remains a start by necessity, but he is the most likely candidate to underperform his baseline if he cannot navigate Early\u2019s elite pitching profile early in the game.",
